### **Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)**
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "NighttimeUrbanFloodedRoad" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :StateAnomaly ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasObstacle :obstacle1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2, :risk3 ;
    :hasEvidence :evidence1 .

:weather1 a :RainyCondition ;
    :description "Heavy rain causing flooded road conditions" .

:obstacle1 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "Large puddle/standing water covering road surface" .

:evidence1 a :FallingObjectIndicator ;
    :description "Water droplets visible in headlights, indicating active rainfall" ;
    :indicatesPotentialRisk :risk3 .

:risk1 a :RoadConditionRisk ;
    :description "Slippery road surface due to standing water and rain" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Reduced visibility of traffic signs and distant vehicles due to rain" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:risk3 a :WeatherRisk ;
    :description "Active rainfall increasing collision risk" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev3 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.9"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .

:sev3 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.8"^^xsd:float .
```

